class Solution {
public:
    vector<int> insertionSort(vector<int>& nums) {
        int n = nums.size();

        for(int i = 0; i<n ;i++){ // taversing full array
            int j = i;   // taking 0th index in first iter, 0th and 1st index in second...

            while(j>0 && nums[j - 1] > nums[j]){ // j > 0, because
            // left most case...at index 1 compared with index 0.
            // at index 1 comparing with index 0-1...not possible.

                swap(nums[j - 1], nums[j]);
                j--;
            }
        }
        return nums;
    }
};

```

## Complexity
**Time Complexity:** 
- **Best Case:** `O(n)` (array already sorted)
- **Average Case:** `O(n²)`
- **Worst Case:** `O(n²)` (array sorted in reverse order)

**Space Complexity:** - `O(1)` (In-place sorting)

